I stand by that.  It would be neat if jewelry shop keepers did
buy and sell all gems at actual value (after the usual
adjustments for markup and surcharges and whatnot just like for
non-gem items), because they have a touchstone (and are
presumably experts in the field and could therefore use an
uncursed touchstone as blessed) and thus would know what the gems
are actually worth.  It would be neat, but it's not a very
high-priority enhancement because it would have relatively little
impact on gameplay most of the time.

> Although arguably perhaps they should buy glass for a very
> small price too, in the hopes that they might be able to sell
> it to a sucker for thousands...

Presumably they can obtain a nearly unlimited supply of worthless
glass for very little outlay, without buying it from you.  That's
why it's worthless.

I do think it's slightly odd that shopkeepers never restock if
you buy up all their stuff.  I understand the gameplay rationale
for this (changing it could be unbalancing), but that doesn't
stop it from being slightly odd.


